course: dictionary
lesson: 11664
title: A formal word: assailant
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An assailant is a person who attacks someone physically, which means they use force on someone's body. It is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in the news, in police reports and in court cases, not in everyday chat.
explain: Use the context to work out what it means. «The assailant ran off before the police arrived.» Ran off and police tell you that something bad happened and that a person harmed someone. The assailant is that person.
explain: Look for common phrases. «The assailant fled» means the attacker ran away. «An unknown assailant» means nobody knows who the attacker is. «Describe the assailant» means tell the police what the attacker looked like.
fact: An assailant is a person who attacks someone physically.
fact: Assailant is a noun. Its plural is assailants.
fact: Assailant is a formal word, used in news, police reports and court cases.
fact: «The assailant fled» means the attacker ran away.
fact: «An unknown assailant» means an attacker whose identity is not known.
exercise: «The police asked the witness to describe the assailant.» What does assailant mean here? | A police officer on duty | A kind neighbour | A witness who saw the event | *A person who attacks someone
exercise: «The assailant fled before anyone could stop him.» What does fled mean? | *Ran away | Stood still | Shouted loudly | Fell asleep
exercise: «Police are searching for an unknown assailant.» Why does the report say unknown? | *Nobody knows who the attacker is | The attacker is famous and everyone knows them | The attacker is a child | The attacker was very kind
test: In a news report: «The assailant was wearing a grey coat.» What is an assailant? | A thief who only takes bags | *A person who attacks someone physically | A police station | A coat seller
test: Which sentence uses assailant correctly? | «My assailant and I went swimming together.» | *«The assailant ran off after hurting the shopkeeper.» | «The assailant baked a big chocolate cake for his friends.»
exam: What does «an unknown assailant» mean? | *A person who attacked someone, but whose name is not known | A person who was never seen by anyone at all | A famous person whom everyone recognises | A friend who helped the police
